---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ProjectGrid from '../components/ProjectGrid';
import { Code2, ArrowLeft, Terminal, Package, Cpu } from 'lucide-react';
---

<Layout
  title="Open Source Projects & Rust Crates | Jeric Bas"
  description="Explore my public npm packages, Rust systems utilities, and architectural prototypes."
>
  <div class="mb-8">
    <a
      href="/"
      class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-secondary-theme hover:text-primary-theme transition-colors mb-4"
    >
      <ArrowLeft className="w-3.5 h-3.5" />
      Back to Home
    </a>
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
      <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-surface-elevated border border-theme flex items-center justify-center">
        <Code2 className="w-4 h-4 accent-text" />
      </div>
      <div>
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-primary-theme">Rust & npm Craft</h1>
        <p class="text-sm text-secondary-theme mt-1">
          Open-source developer tooling, system monitors, and libraries built for performance and reliability.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-12">
    <ProjectGrid client:load filter="all" />
  </div>

  <!-- Engineering Philosophy Note -->
  <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl border border-theme bg-surface-elevated text-xs text-secondary-theme leading-relaxed">
    <h3 class="font-bold text-sm text-primary-theme mb-2 flex items-center gap-2">
      <Terminal className="w-4 h-4 accent-text" />
      My Open-Source Engineering Principles
    </h3>
    <p class="mb-2">
      <strong>Zero Unnecessary Overhead:</strong> CLI utilities and plugins must start instantaneously. If a tool lags before processing input, developer trust diminishes.
    </p>
    <p class="mb-2">
      <strong>Predictable Dependencies:</strong> Whether publishing to npm or crates.io, keeping the transitive dependency tree shallow prevents supply chain rot and ecosystem conflicts.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Building in the Open:</strong> Every tool here was born out of genuine friction encountered while building software.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
